From: Charles DuBose <kayakyakr@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:54:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tu: report the process-wide heap usage in the memory budget

VK_EXT_memory_budget's heapUsage counts one Vulkan instance's allocations,
since each instance enumerates its own physical device. A D3D12 game under
Proton allocates through vkd3d-proton's instance but reads its usage through
DXVK's DXGI, whose instance allocates nothing: Diablo IV logged 0 MB used
against a budget that shrank with the system's free memory, never trimmed,
and Android killed it.

One driver library is loaded per process, so a counter beside heap.used,
added where Turnip adds to and takes from it, covers every instance.
heapUsage reports that counter and the budget is computed from it; heap.used
still guards each instance's heap size.

Signed-off-by: Charles DuBose <kayakyakr@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
index e8ef940..10e8efa 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_device.cc
@@ -2114,6 +2114,8 @@ tu_get_system_heap_size(struct tu_physical_device *physical_device)
    return available_ram;
 }
 
+static uint64_t tu_process_heap_used;
+
 static inline VkDeviceSize
 tu_get_budget_memory(struct tu_physical_device *physical_device)
 {
@@ -2156,7 +2158,7 @@ tu_GetPhysicalDeviceMemoryProperties2(VkPhysicalDevice pdev,
       case VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_PHYSICAL_DEVICE_MEMORY_BUDGET_PROPERTIES_EXT: {
          VkPhysicalDeviceMemoryBudgetPropertiesEXT *memory_budget_props =
             (VkPhysicalDeviceMemoryBudgetPropertiesEXT *) ext;
-         memory_budget_props->heapUsage[0] = physical_device->heap.used;
+         memory_budget_props->heapUsage[0] = p_atomic_read(&tu_process_heap_used);
          memory_budget_props->heapBudget[0] = tu_get_budget_memory(physical_device);
 
          /* The heapBudget and heapUsage values must be zero for array elements
@@ -3509,6 +3511,7 @@ tu_add_to_heap(struct tu_device *dev, struct tu_bo *bo)
       return vk_errorf(dev, VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY,
                        "Out of heap memory");
    }
+   p_atomic_add(&tu_process_heap_used, bo->size);
    return VK_SUCCESS;
 }
 
@@ -3597,6 +3600,7 @@ _tu_destroy_memory(struct tu_device *device,
 {
    if (mem->bo) {
       p_atomic_add(&device->physical_device->heap.used, -mem->bo->size);
+      p_atomic_add(&tu_process_heap_used, -mem->bo->size);
       tu_bo_finish(device, mem->bo);
    }
 
